<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <!--
    Privacy manifest for the Minimum Stress app target.

    Place this at ios/App/App/PrivacyInfo.xcprivacy on the mobile-app branch and
    add it to the "App" target's Copy Bundle Resources. The app is a Capacitor
    shell that loads the production web app; it runs no advertising or analytics
    SDK, so it does not track.

    - NSPrivacyTracking: false, and no tracking domains — do NOT add an ATT prompt.
    - NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes is intentionally empty here: data collection
      happens server-side through the web app and is disclosed in the App Store
      Connect App Privacy label (see docs/app-store/privacy-label.md), which is the
      authoritative source. If App Store validation asks for the types mirrored in
      the manifest, populate them from privacy-label.md.
    - Required-reason API: Capacitor and WKWebView read/write UserDefaults for
      same-app state (reason CA92.1). Verify against the final plugin set and add
      any additional reasons your bundled plugins require.
    - Each bundled Capacitor plugin / third-party SDK (and Stripe, if the native
      SDK is added later) must ship its own PrivacyInfo.xcprivacy; confirm they are
      present during `cap sync ios` before archiving.
  -->
  <key>NSPrivacyTracking</key>
  <false/>
  <key>NSPrivacyTrackingDomains</key>
  <array/>
  <key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes</key>
  <array/>
  <key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes</key>
  <array>
    <dict>
      <key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPIType</key>
      <string>NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryUserDefaults</string>
      <key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypeReasons</key>
      <array>
        <string>CA92.1</string>
      </array>
    </dict>
  </array>
</dict>
</plist>
